    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d506">

                <pb facs="0807" n="703" sameAs="frus:frus1933v02/pg703"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">652.116/23</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Spain (Flack) to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1189</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-05-17">May 17,
                        1933</date>.<lb/>[Received May 27.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Adverting to my telegram of May 13, 12
                    noon (1933),<anchor n="23" xml:id="d506-f1"/> I have the honor to enclose in
                    quintuplicate the Spanish text with translation of the Decree, dated May 9, and
                    published in the <hi rendition="#italic">Gaceta de Madrid</hi> of May 11 on this
                        subject.<anchor n="24" xml:id="d506-f2"/> The translation was kindly
                    furnished by the office of the Commercial Attaché.</p>
                <p>The two Articles of the short Decree are prefaced with an explanation of the
                    reasons for its issuance, which assert its temporary nature. According to
                    Article 1, Section (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>), the “benefits” (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">retornos</hi>) are to be determined on the statistical
                    results of completed quarters.</p>
                <p>On the morning of May 13, I called to see Señor Doussinague, Political and
                    Commercial Director in the Ministry of State, to seek such additional
                    information as he might care to give me about the Decree, and telephoned him
                    later for a further interpretation. A copy of the Memorandum of the
                    conversations is enclosed.<anchor n="23" xml:id="d506-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>It should be noted in Section (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) of Article 1, that
                    the amount of the benefit to be obtained is not fixed but may not exceed 35%.
                    The amount is undoubtedly intentionally undefined to provide an additional
                    bargaining point in the special agreements which I was informed would be
                    essential to claiming the benefits.</p>
                <p>I shall report promptly any additional information concerning the Decree and its
                    application as it becomes available.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph Flack</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
